---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import IndustryResources from '../../components/IndustryResources.astro';
import RosemarySelection from '../../components/RosemarySelection.astro';
import ApplicationTasks from '../../components/ApplicationTasks.astro';
---
<PageLayout title="Food Applications" lang="en" heroTitle="Food Applications" heroSubtitle="From application conditions to a purchasing specification">
<ApplicationTasks lang="en" industry="food" />
<section class="section-padding"><div class="container-wide max-w-4xl">
<p class="text-xl text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-10">Check ingredient identity and permitted use for the food category and destination market before evaluating processing performance.</p>
<h2 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold mb-6">Troubleshooting and validation</h2><div class="space-y-5">
<div class="p-6 bg-off-white rounded-xl"><h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">Uneven distribution</h3><p class="mt-2 text-gray-600">Compare particle size, premixing, carrier and dosing sequence. Check blend uniformity at pilot scale rather than relying only on a small bench sample.</p></div>
<div class="p-6 bg-off-white rounded-xl"><h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">Flavor or color loss after processing</h3><p class="mt-2 text-gray-600">Evaluate the complete recipe across actual heat, moisture and storage conditions. Define acceptable sensory and appearance limits before scaling up.</p></div>
<div class="p-6 bg-off-white rounded-xl"><h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">Specification mismatch</h3><p class="mt-2 text-gray-600">Request carrier and allergen information and relevant contaminant limits. Confirm labeling and ingredient eligibility with the team responsible for your target market.</p></div>
</div><div class="mt-10 p-8 bg-primary/5 rounded-xl"><h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">What to include in your brief</h2><p class="mt-3 text-gray-700">Food category, recipe context, process conditions, use level, allergen restrictions, packaging and market.</p><p class="mt-3 text-gray-600">Also include the ingredient, first order quantity and documents needed. Grades, samples and documents are subject to availability; certification and regulatory suitability require product- and market-specific review. These are evaluation considerations, not a formulation or suitability guarantee.</p><a href="/request-quote?request=application&amp;source=food&amp;application=food" class="inline-block mt-5 px-6 py-3 bg-primary text-white rounded-lg">Discuss application requirements</a><a href="/resources/downloads" class="inline-block mt-5 ml-4 text-primary underline">Get the sourcing checklist</a></div>
</div></section>
<section class="section-padding"><div class="container-wide max-w-4xl"><h2 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold"><a class="text-primary underline" href="/resources/blog/paprika-extract-format-selection">Paprika colour: choose the material format</a></h2><p class="mt-4 text-gray-600">Compare oil-standardized extracts and water-dispersible preparations, with colour and pungency specified separately.</p></div></section>
<RosemarySelection lang="en" />
<IndustryResources lang="en" industry="food" />
<section class="section-padding"><div class="container-wide max-w-4xl"><h2 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold"><a class="text-primary underline" href="/resources/blog/chicory-fibre-selection">Chicory fibre: select for the formulation task</a></h2><p class="mt-4 text-gray-600">Distinguish dispersibility, solubility and texture development, then compare quotations on an as-supplied fibre basis.</p></div></section>
<section data-cocoa-discovery class="section-padding"><div class="container-wide max-w-4xl"><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold"><a class="underline text-primary" href="/resources/blog/cocoa-selection">Cocoa powder or cocoa extract? Match chocolate character and flavanol delivery separately</a></h2><p class="mt-4 text-gray-700">Compare cocoa powder, flavanol-preserving powder and assayed extracts by chocolate character, composition and the finished formulation.</p></div></section>
<section data-ginger-discovery class="section-padding"><div class="container-wide max-w-4xl"><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold"><a class="underline text-primary" href="/resources/blog/ginger-selection">Choosing processed ginger: why more shogaol does not settle the aroma question</a></h2><p class="mt-4 text-gray-700">Choose ginger by aroma and warming sensation separately, with study-specific drying, extraction and carrier evidence.</p></div></section>
<section data-beetroot-discovery class="section-padding"><div class="container-wide max-w-4xl"><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold"><a class="underline text-primary" href="/resources/blog/beetroot-product-formats">Beetroot powder product development: what three Amazon listings reveal</a></h2><p class="mt-4 text-gray-700">Three seller-displayed beet products show different food, bulk-mixing and flavoured-drink briefs, without ranking efficacy or demand.</p></div></section>
<section data-beetroot-discovery class="section-padding"><div class="container-wide max-w-4xl"><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold"><a class="underline text-primary" href="/resources/blog/beet-colour-plant-based-meat">Why does beet-red plant-based meat stay red after cooking? Where sugar beet pectin and laccase fit</a></h2><p class="mt-4 text-gray-700">Compare shade adjustment with beet-red, sugar beet pectin and laccase research for cooking colour transitions in plant-based meat.</p></div></section>
<section data-olive-pectin class="section-padding"><div class="container-wide max-w-4xl"><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold"><a class="underline text-primary" href="/resources/blog/olive-leaf-beverage-encapsulation">Olive leaf extract in acidic drinks: when liposomes help—and when they do not</a></h2><p class="mt-4 text-gray-700">Compare olive-leaf powder specifications, three retail formulations and refrigerated beverage evidence before choosing liposomal encapsulation.</p></div></section>
<section data-olive-pectin class="section-padding"><div class="container-wide max-w-4xl"><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold"><a class="underline text-primary" href="/resources/blog/citrus-pectin-gel-selection">Low-sugar citrus pectin: match the setting window, calcium response and texture</a></h2><p class="mt-4 text-gray-700">Compare seven named citrus pectin grades, calcium response and setting behaviour for low-sugar spreads and acidified protein drinks.</p></div></section>
<section data-oat-apple class="section-padding"><div class="container-wide max-w-4xl"><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold"><a class="underline text-primary" href="/resources/blog/oat-beta-glucan-material-selection">Oat beta-glucan for drinks: do not buy molecular weight in isolation</a></h2><p class="mt-4 text-gray-700">Compare oat beta-glucan molecular weight, historical assay viscosity and current ingredient forms before selecting a drink ingredient.</p></div></section>
<section data-oat-apple class="section-padding"><div class="container-wide max-w-4xl"><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold"><a class="underline text-primary" href="/resources/blog/apple-extract-phloridzin-fibre-pectin">Apple extract, phloridzin, fibre or pectin: choose the ingredient before comparing the assay</a></h2><p class="mt-4 text-gray-700">Distinguish apple polyphenol extracts, phloridzin ingredients, functional apple fibre and pectin using primary research and named supplier examples.</p></div></section>
</PageLayout>
